(27451,2126,N'mirror',N'cái gương',N'/ˈmɪr.ɚ/',N'A2',1,N'2023-09-08T13:48:35.1520000',NULL,NULL),
(59489,2126,N'Mirror',N'1) Do you like looking at yourself in the mirror? How often? Yes, I do, but not excessively. I usually check a few times a day, mainly when I’m getting ready. It’s just to make sure I look neat and presentable. 2) Do you usually take a mirror with you? No, I don’t usually carry a mirror with me. If I need one, I just use my phone camera because it’s more practical. It does the same job and saves space. 3) Have you ever bought mirrors? Yes, I have. I once bought a small mirror for my study desk because the design was simple and looked good quality. It’s been useful for quick checks. 4) Would you use mirrors to decorate your room? Yes, I would. Mirrors can make a room feel brighter and more spacious. So they’re both decorative and practical.',NULL,NULL,1,N'2026-05-16T00:13:16.6530000',NULL,NULL),
(59490,2126,N'Mirror',N'1) Do you like looking at yourself in the mirror? How often? Absolutely. When I look in the mirror, it gives me a confidence boost because I like what I see. It’s not just about my appearance—it also feels like a quick moment of self-reflection. So if I need to reset my mindset, I’ll take a short look. 2) Do you usually take a mirror with you? No, not at all. Carrying a mirror around makes me seem overly obsessed with my looks. To me, it can even signal insecurity, like I’m worried about being judged. So I think keeping a mirror in my pocket is a bad idea. 3) Have you ever bought mirrors? Yes, but not for myself. I once bought a mirror as a Women’s Day gift for my mum. It felt meaningful because it carried the message that she’s beautiful. So it was more like a reminder than just an object. 4) Would you use mirrors to decorate your room? Never. I might use a mirror in a public restroom, but I don’t like having one in my room. It just makes me uncomfortable, even if I can’t fully explain why. So overall, I don’t decorate with mirrors and I don’t keep one at home.',NULL,NULL,1,N'2026-05-16T00:14:27.6700000',NULL,NULL),
(59491,2126,N'Mirror',N'1) Do you like looking at yourself in the mirror? How often? Yes, absolutely. Whenever I walk past a mirror, I usually pause for around 15 to 30 seconds to admire my reflection. It gives me a quick confidence boost, especially before I leave the house. It’s become a small habit that puts me in a good mood. 2) Do you usually take a mirror with you? No, I don’t normally carry a mirror with me. To be honest, it makes me feel a bit “girly,” and I’m not really into that image. But if it’s a special occasion and I need to look polished, I’ll bring one just in case. Otherwise, I can manage without it. 3) Have you ever bought mirrors? Yes, I have. I remember buying a lovely mirror as a gift for someone I used to care about a lot. I felt genuinely happy when they accepted it and seemed pleased. It wasn’t expensive, but it meant something. 4) Would you use mirrors to decorate your room? Of course. I’d like a small mirror in my room because it’s both practical and a nice decoration. I’d probably keep it on my desk so it’s easy to use when I’m getting ready. And honestly, it’s also fun to see my face every day, so yes—I’d definitely have one.',NULL,NULL,1,N'2026-05-16T00:14:39.2010000',NULL,NULL),
